+For an installation outside the checkout, run `npm pack` here; its prepack step
+builds the archive. Install that local `.tgz` into your own project. In bash or zsh,
+replace both absolute paths below, then define a launcher for the installed beta:
+
+```sh
+cd /absolute/path/to/your/project
+npm install /absolute/path/to/archive.tgz
+MORI_BETA_PKG="$PWD/node_modules/@moriarty-lang/beta"
+mori() { node "$MORI_BETA_PKG/dist/cli.js" "$@"; }
+mori init invoice
+cd invoice
+mori check invoice.mori --json
+mori test .
+mori simulate invoice.mori --action pay --scenario scenario.json
+```
+
+The `invoice` directory must not exist yet. Keep using the same terminal: the
+function selects the installed beta CLI even after changing directories, so the
+starter README's `mori` commands need no global install or repository metadata.
+In a new terminal, return to your install project and define the function again.
+`npx mori` is also available from that install project. No npm registry publication
+is claimed. These local examples still return **PreparedUnqualified**.
 `mori COMMAND --help` shows the command's arguments. Exit 0 means the requested
 local operation completed: a preparation remains unqualified. Exit 1 means
 rejection, unsupported execution, test mismatch or a command/file error.
